/-!
# The derived lower shriek of modules for the flat-fppf site (Stacks 07AS, part (4))

Let `𝒳` be an algebraic stack and let `g : Sh(𝒳_{flat,fppf}) ⟶ Sh(𝒳_{fppf})` be the morphism of
ringed topoi of **Stacks 0788** (2), whose inverse image on sheaves of modules is restriction to
the flat objects, `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.moduleRestriction`. **Stacks 07AS** part (4)
asserts that the lower shriek `g_! : Mod(𝒪_{𝒳_{flat,fppf}}) ⥤ Mod(𝒪_𝒳)` has a left derived functor

`Lg_! : D(𝒪_{𝒳_{flat,fppf}}) ⟶ D(𝒪_𝒳)`,

left adjoint to `g^*` and with `g^* Lg_! = id`. All three are proved here, with no hypothesis.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.derivedModuleLowerShriek`: `Lg_!`, the total left derived
  functor of `g_!` on the unbounded derived categories.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.derivedModuleLowerShriekAdjunction`:
  `Lg_! ⊣ g^*`, the right adjoint being
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.derivedModuleRestriction`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.derivedModuleLowerShriekRestrictionIso`: `g^* Lg_! ≅ id`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.hasPointwiseLeftDerivedFunctor_moduleLowerShriek`:
  **Stacks 07AS (4)**, existence of `Lg_!`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.isIso_derivedModuleLowerShriekAdjunction_unit`:
  **Stacks 07AS (4)**, the unit of `Lg_! ⊣ g^*` is invertible, i.e. `g^* Lg_! = id`.

## Implementation notes

As in the source, the proof is Stacks 07AC for the inclusion of the flat objects: the criterion of
Stacks 0794 reduces existence and adjointness to the acyclicity of `g_!` on bounded above acyclic
complexes of direct sums of the `j_{U!} 𝒪_U`, which is Stacks 0D6X. The sites are not small but
essentially small;
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedLowerShriek.lowerShriekModules_acyclic_of_essentiallySmall` provides that
acyclicity by transport to small models, and
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedLowerShriek.hasPointwiseLeftDerivedLowerShriek_of_essentiallySmall` runs
the criterion. The final assertion is read off from the underived `g^* g_! = id`
(`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedLowerShriek.isIso_adjunctionModules_unit`, the inclusion being fully
faithful) by `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedLowerShriek.isIso_derivedLowerShriekAdjunction_unit`.

Everything is stated for arbitrary models `[HasDerivedCategory]` of the two derived categories,
and `g^*` is `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.derivedModuleRestriction`, the functor of
**Stacks 07B9** (2)(b).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07AS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07AS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07AC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07AC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0788](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0788)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0789](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0789)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0794](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0794)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D6X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D6X)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

